From: FlipperEmu
Subject: [PATCH] stm32l4x5_usart: tell the board of a character nobody heard

While the receiver is off (UE or RE clear) the model takes a character
from its backend and drops it, as the hardware does not sample its RX
pin then. The pin has had the character's start bit all the same, and a
guest may watch that pin as a GPIO while it keeps the UART's receiver
off: to wake up on the first edge, or to be called by what is wired to
it. The model had no way to tell a board that anything had come.

The device has a GPIO output "rx-unheard" now, pulsed once for each
character that came while the receiver was off. A board that models the
RX pin can put a start bit on it; a board that does not connect the line
behaves as before.

Seen with the Flipper Zero firmware: it waits for an expansion module
with the receiver of the module's UART off and an interrupt on the
falling edge of its RX pin, and the module begins with a short low level
there. Nothing sent to the port could reach that interrupt.

Signed-off-by: FlipperEmu
---
--- a/hw/char/stm32l4x5_usart.c
+++ b/hw/char/stm32l4x5_usart.c
@@ -353,6 +353,11 @@
     if (!usart_rx_enabled(s)) {
         trace_stm32l4x5_usart_receiver_not_enabled(
             FIELD_EX32(s->cr1, CR1, UE), FIELD_EX32(s->cr1, CR1, RE));
+        /*
+         * The UART drops it, but its start bit was on the RX pin all the
+         * same: for a board whose guest watches that pin as a GPIO.
+         */
+        qemu_irq_pulse(s->rx_unheard);
         return;
     }
 
@@ -695,6 +700,7 @@
 
     sysbus_init_irq(SYS_BUS_DEVICE(obj), &s->irq);
     qdev_init_gpio_out_named(DEVICE(obj), &s->dma_rx, "dma-rx", 1);
+    qdev_init_gpio_out_named(DEVICE(obj), &s->rx_unheard, "rx-unheard", 1);
     timer_init_ns(&s->rx_timer, QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL, usart_rx_timer, s);
     timer_init_ns(&s->idle_timer, QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL, usart_idle_timer, s);
 
--- a/include/hw/char/stm32l4x5_usart.h
+++ b/include/hw/char/stm32l4x5_usart.h
@@ -58,6 +58,7 @@
     CharFrontend chr;
     qemu_irq irq;
     qemu_irq dma_rx;        /* a character waits, and the DMA is to take it */
+    qemu_irq rx_unheard;    /* a character came while the receiver was off */
     guint watch_tag;
 
     /* Reception at the line's speed, and the idle line after it */
